{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations","id":1066567,"title":"On infiltrations","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-22T14:01:39-07:00","id":1066567,"title":"On infiltrations","content":"I was wondering. Participants of CoW are always aware of it happening, right? So in the case of entering Consilium building or cabals Sanktum I think it should be customary to drop all Veils to make sure that there is no CoW which would give away that you are hiding it. Or at least let the searching party to pierce it. <br /> And that's it. Either you have nothing to hide or you are unwelcome as a potential doppelganger. <br /> I don't have a book on me but the Masque merit doesn't seem to change your body so it won't help in this problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T04:54:52-07:00","id":1066777,"title":"","content":"I was reading the introductory fiction from Silver Ladder book, the one about the Nemean, and I find it impossible to recreate under 2E. Even if you win on a CoW against a lesser mage he will know that there was one and you are hiding something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:08:19-07:00","id":1066782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations#post1066567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was wondering. Participants of CoW are always aware of it happening, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not so sure... If somebody tries to penetrate Veiling with CoW, there is Clash of Wills. But if participants of CoW are always aware of it happening, they will always know that &quot;there is something Veiled here&quot;, which kinda beats the purpose. Personally, I don't even ping active spells (not casting, but active spells) with Peripheral Mage Sight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:17:35-07:00","id":1066787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>p.118</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages may spend Willpower to bolster the contested roll,<br /> and <b>are always aware</b> when their spells are clashing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they were not aware they couldn't spend WP on it. It says spells I guess it applies to all CoW instances. So if for example mage is unconscious he can't take part in it and automatically fails. When they asleep they might be woken by it I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:37:23-07:00","id":1066797,"title":"","content":"The magical effect itself isn't dependent on the mage being conscious so CoW should still apply.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:44:37-07:00","id":1066798,"title":"","content":"Might be true but I'm sure you can't spend WP when passed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T05:51:18-07:00","id":1066801,"title":"","content":"That I do agree with. I just think a spell shouldn't lose effect because the mage is unconscious considering that spells remain even after the death of the mage, though unsafely relinquished if not previously safely relinquished. Clash of Wills doesn't actually have much to do with wills outside the possibility of spending Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:08:50-07:00","id":1066805,"title":"","content":"1) If you lose the CoW you can't be sure you were actually attempting to penetrate a Veil. 2) Even if you're pretty sure, you don't know what's hidden and depending on the circumstances this might be all that the person who set up the Veil needs to further misdirect you or come up with some other countermeasures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:27:11-07:00","id":1066809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066805#post1066805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) If you lose the CoW you can't be sure you were actually attempting to penetrate a Veil. 2) Even if you're pretty sure, you don't know what's hidden and depending on the circumstances this might be all that the person who set up the Veil needs to further misdirect you or come up with some other countermeasures.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Since they didn't lose the CoW, which they should do, you know that they are hiding something. If they insist on hiding something they are a threat. 2. The only way to do it would be to mess with memories of the searching party and you would have to do it in that same moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T06:47:35-07:00","id":1066826,"title":"","content":"Am gon doo a spel fo it.<br /> <br /> <b>Under the Bushel (Mind 2)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Veiling<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Duration<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <br /> This spell hides will of the subject from others making it impossible to be aware of CoW against them. Others also can't spend Willpower on the test. ST makes a hidden roll of Power Stat + Power for an unaware participants.<br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> By blurring the edges of mages will the spell assures victory in uncertain circumstances. In the case of a draw the subject wins or rather the opponent loses by giving up too early.</span><br /> <b>+1 Reach: </b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Instead of veiling the CoW completely this spell change's the apparent outcome to &quot;Won&quot;.<br /> Kind of like Shield of Chronos?</span><br /> <br /> But it's not RAW and not many gm's would allow it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-24-2017, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:03:13-07:00","id":1066838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066809#post1066809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Since they didn't lose the CoW, which they should do, you know that they are hiding something. If they insist on hiding something they are a threat. 2. The only way to do it would be to mess with memories of the searching party and you would have to do it in that same moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>They know they had a CoW, they don't necessarily know why it happened though. Also, messing with their memory is just one option available to you when you choose to respond to someone clashing with your Veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:10:36-07:00","id":1066845,"title":"","content":"Well. If you are at an airport and the machine beeps the guards know that you have something unwanted/forbidden. And you can't enter the plane as long as the machine beeps on you. Period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:32:55-07:00","id":1066861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066838#post1066838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, messing with their memory is just one option available to you when you choose to respond to someone clashing with your Veil.</div> </div> </div> </div>And frankly without examples this isn't an argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:35:11-07:00","id":1066863,"title":"","content":"Sure, teleport the subject of the Veil away for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T07:50:33-07:00","id":1066874,"title":"","content":"What? I don't understand.<br /> <br /> Lets make some background. We have a Spy that has loaded Veilings to be identical to a Compromised Cabalmate which now is hidden away in some folded shadow pocket. The Spy arrives at the door of Enemy Sanctum to steer the conversation of culprits to confession. They are in a middle of planning a treason so they send Obrimos to check the aura signatures of Spy.<br /> Obrimos fails on CoW and sees the forged Nimbus, but he know that he failed a CoW. He says: &quot; C'mon, you know the drill. Let me in.&quot;<br /> The Spy responds with: &quot;?????&quot;<br /> <br /> ???? - teleport away?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:43:22-07:00","id":1066903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066874#post1066874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? I don't understand.<br /> <br /> Lets make some background. We have a Spy that has loaded Veilings to be identical to a Compromised Cabalmate which now is hidden away in some folded shadow pocket. The Spy arrives at the door of Enemy Sanctum to steer the conversation of culprits to confession. They are in a middle of planning a treason so they send Obrimos to check the aura signatures of Spy.<br /> Obrimos fails on CoW and sees the forged Nimbus, but he know that he failed a CoW. He says: &quot; C'mon, you know the drill. Let me in.&quot;<br /> The Spy responds with: &quot;?????&quot;<br /> <br /> ???? - teleport away?</div> </div> </div> </div>...yeah, that just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> &quot;You know you are having a clash of wills,&quot; for things like, when your Mind Shield protects you from a Telepathic Attack or something.<br /> <br /> If you know that your attempt to read someone's aura signature provoked a clash of wills, then you might as well not bother HAVING spells that do things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:54:23-07:00","id":1066910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066903#post1066903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...yeah, that just doesn't work.<br /> <br /> &quot;You know you are having a clash of wills,&quot; for things like, when your Mind Shield protects you from a Telepathic Attack or something.<br /> <br /> If you know that your attempt to read someone's aura signature provoked a clash of wills, then you might as well not bother HAVING spells that do things like that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. Once again &quot;Mages may spend Willpower to bolster the contested roll, and <b>are always aware</b> when their spells are clashing.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:56:26-07:00","id":1066916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066874#post1066874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? I don't understand.<br /> <br /> Lets make some background. We have a Spy that has loaded Veilings to be identical to a Compromised Cabalmate which now is hidden away in some folded shadow pocket. The Spy arrives at the door of Enemy Sanctum to steer the conversation of culprits to confession. They are in a middle of planning a treason so they send Obrimos to check the aura signatures of Spy.<br /> Obrimos fails on CoW and sees the forged Nimbus, but he know that he failed a CoW. He says: &amp;quot; C'mon, you know the drill. Let me in.&amp;quot;<br /> The Spy responds with: &amp;quot;?????&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> ???? - teleport away?</div> </div> </div> </div>In that instance, no, teleporting wouldn't work. Obviously. I was speaking generally after all.<br /> <br /> In that specific instance you'd be smarter to set up decoy Veils beforehand that you can drop while dissuading them from looking more closely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T08:58:31-07:00","id":1066918,"title":"","content":"Veiling spells are best used to make a thing appear not worth looking at in the first place. They do start to fall down on the job if a Mage starts looking for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:05:53-07:00","id":1066922,"title":"","content":"The obvious solution is to offer spells like that a Reach option, probably just +1 if we're honest, to have the clash of wills that they provoke not be obvious to the other Mage.<br /> <br /> ...I'm somewhat hesitant to make a spell that's largely useless without its Reach option, admittedly, but honestly there are probably options where simply 'obviously covering up something' is all that you actually need to do.<br /> <br /> Edit for Clarity: <i>This would not be a generic Reach option for anything. It'd only exist for spells that are radically less useful when being used for their primary purpose, such as the specific spells talked about in this thread when used for infiltration.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":728,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","user":"CrownedSun","date":". 03-23-2017, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:06:45-07:00","id":1066924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066916#post1066916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In that instance, no, teleporting wouldn't work. Obviously. I was speaking generally after all.<br /> <br /> In that specific instance you'd be smarter to set up decoy Veils beforehand that you can drop while dissuading them from looking more closely.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the Spy has two spells on his aura. First changes it to the exact copy of the Compromised Cabalmate and the second changes Veils that copy. Obrimos checks, sees no aura and senses that he failed a CoW. &quot;Show me your aura&quot; he says. The Spy laughs &quot;Sorry, I forgot&quot;. In the next attempt Obrimos pierces the lowered Veil and stares directly at the changed aura. He gets a CoW and senses that he failed. &quot;Wtf, Mike? Let me in&quot; he says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:09:10-07:00","id":1066926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066922#post1066922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The obvious solution is to offer spells like that a Reach option, probably just +1 if we're honest, to have the clash of wills that they provoke not be obvious to the other Mage.<br /> <br /> ...I'm somewhat hesitant to make a spell that's largely useless without its Reach option, admittedly, but honestly there are probably options where simply 'obviously covering up something' is all that you actually need to do.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, but I'm talking about RAW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:10:16-07:00","id":1066927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066926#post1066926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know, but I'm talking about RAW.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not really a meaningful distinction to make when the RAW produces a situation that doesn't work.<br /> <br /> That's how RPG's are written.<br /> <br /> the Count of Words and all that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/728-crownedsun","name":"CrownedSun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar728_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"217"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:16:02-07:00","id":1066931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrownedSun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066927#post1066927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not really a meaningful distinction to make when the RAW produces a situation that doesn't work.<br /> <br /> That's how RPG's are written.<br /> <br /> the Count of Words and all that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well. It seems to be an intent. Participants of CoW are aware of it happening, by RAW. I try to go around the rules in my hacks, not against them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:18:53-07:00","id":1066934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066924#post1066924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the Spy has two spells on his aura. First changes it to the exact copy of the Compromised Cabalmate and the second changes Veils that copy. Obrimos checks, sees no aura and senses that he failed a CoW. &amp;quot;Show me your aura&amp;quot; he says. The Spy laughs &amp;quot;Sorry, I forgot&amp;quot;. In the next attempt Obrimos pierces the lowered Veil and stares directly at the changed aura. He gets a CoW and senses that he failed. &amp;quot;Wtf, Mike? Let me in&amp;quot; he says.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you could make a spell which falsifies the information received on a failed CoW such that they appear to have succeeded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:24:16-07:00","id":1066939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066934#post1066934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you could make a spell which falsifies the information received on a failed CoW such that they appear to have succeeded.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Maybe a Reach effect for my spell from this thread? +1 Reach: Instead of veiling the CoW completely this spell change's the apparent outcome to &quot;Won&quot;. Kind of like Shield of Chronos?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:25:38-07:00","id":1066940,"title":"","content":"There's a lot of openness to interpretation in the rules. Mages are always aware when their spells are Clashed but Mage Sight is not a spell; a Clash tells you something resisted you, but you don't know if you succeeded or failed, etc.<br /> <br /> As for dropping spells when entering a sanctum, that feels like good manners, yeah. Natural courtesy.<br /> <br /> As far as infiltration goes, though, there's lots of methods to do so without a spell. Spells are shortcuts, that's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:29:27-07:00","id":1066942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066940#post1066940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a lot of openness to interpretation in the rules. Mages are always aware when their spells are Clashed but Mage Sight is not a spell; a Clash tells you something resisted you, but you don't know if you succeeded or failed, etc.<br /> <br /> As for dropping spells when entering a sanctum, that feels like good manners, yeah. Natural courtesy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> If you don't know if you succeeded you still know that it happened and it's a sign that there is something. The guest should in this reading of rules get rid of a spell completely.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as infiltration goes, though, there's lots of methods to do so without a spell. Spells are shortcuts, that's all. </div> </div> </div>Can you give an example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:38:22-07:00","id":1066948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1066942#post1066942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you give an example?</div> </div> </div> </div>Invest in Maques, Alternative Identity and a really good makeup artist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T09:41:02-07:00","id":1066953,"title":"","content":"Disguises work for for hiding your physical appearance. Acting works for hiding your mannerisms. If you're in the extreme case where you need to even hide your memories, lock them away in your Oneiros so that even you don't remember them.<br /> <br /> In the end, your average Mage expects spells and magical deception but without the red flag of Mage Sight, they're really not much better than mortals at spotting mundane ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T10:58:01-07:00","id":1067013,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2855_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2855\" data-vbnamecard=\"2855\">Axelgear</a><br /> <br /> Lets assume that you can fool a cabal that you are their member by looking similar, being acting prodigy, having mission impossible level of disguise and dedicating part of your life to .get a specific Masque. It is doable as long as it is Obrimos who greets you in the door. Let it be a Thyrsus who checks your DNA and you are quite fucked. Of course I can see Masque Advanced and Epic but it's still something completely different from 1E.<br /> But the scenario when the Master wishes to infiltrate the cabal (opening fiction from SL book) is impossible. Even if the cabal is made of Initiates. He could just command them too think that they checked him and all that, but it's something different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-23-2017, 02:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:42:17-07:00","id":1067045,"title":"","content":"Obrimos Doorkeeper will look at you with displeased look, because your acting and disguises and other things tripped their Pierce Deception.<br /> <br /> As for the thread question, we just assume that if a Mage lost Clash of Will VS concealment and other stuff like that, they assume there is nothing wrong, instead of &quot;I totally failed in finding something, so I know there is something, ah ha&quot;. It's a homerule, but we feel that it keeps the spirit of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T11:48:54-07:00","id":1067049,"title":"","content":"When your friend meets you at the door, do you ask to see their ID? Theoretically possible doesn't mean likely. You could, theoretically, disguise a tank as a car and hide the disguise under a Prime Veiling spell, but every Mage in the land isn't thinking &quot;HMMM, BETTER MAKE SURE THAT HONDA CIVIC ISN'T AN ABRAMS&quot;.<br /> <br /> People look for what they expect to see. No spy in history has ever had a foolproof plan to hide their activities; they've survived by evading suspicion in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:04:45-07:00","id":1067066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067049#post1067049\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When your friend meets you at the door, do you ask to see their ID? Theoretically possible doesn't mean likely. You could, theoretically, disguise a tank as a car and hide the disguise under a Prime Veiling spell, but every Mage in the land isn't thinking &quot;HMMM, BETTER MAKE SURE THAT HONDA CIVIC ISN'T AN ABRAMS&quot;.<br /> <br /> People look for what they expect to see. No spy in history has ever had a foolproof plan to hide their activities; they've survived by evading suspicion in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my example? Of course they would ID you. They are plotting a treason and know that they can be spied on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:07:33-07:00","id":1067067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067045#post1067045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obrimos Doorkeeper will look at you with displeased look, because your acting and disguises and other things tripped their Pierce Deception.<br /> <br /> As for the thread question, we just assume that if a Mage lost Clash of Will VS concealment and other stuff like that, they assume there is nothing wrong, instead of &quot;I totally failed in finding something, so I know there is something, ah ha&quot;. It's a homerule, but we feel that it keeps the spirit of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats worth of considering as a hack, but it breaks &quot;the immersion&quot;. Roll CoW, you failed and it was nothing - but the players now that there was something.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:14:51-07:00","id":1067081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067066#post1067066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my example? Of course they would ID you. They are plotting a treason and know that they can be spied on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This cuts both ways. The person answering the door doesn't know if the person they're looking at is really them, but the person standing at the door doesn't know if the person they're looking at is a liar in disguise either. Mind-reading magic to confirm their identity could just be secretly a method to confirm treason. Far safer for everyone if they <i>don't</i> use spells and rely on subtle recognition of one another's behaviour.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:42:28-07:00","id":1067102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067081#post1067081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This cuts both ways. The person answering the door doesn't know if the person they're looking at is really them, but the person standing at the door doesn't know if the person they're looking at is a liar in disguise either. Mind-reading magic to confirm their identity could just be secretly a method to confirm treason. Far safer for everyone if they <i>don't</i> use spells and rely on subtle recognition of one another's behaviour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I said that there are other ways of doing this, but now I'm now refering a specific bit of fiction from SL book where the Master changes his body to infiltrate the cabal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T12:58:54-07:00","id":1067119,"title":"","content":"I am aware. Nemean has Prime 3, so he could hide it with a Veiling spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:28:50-07:00","id":1067139,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I don't understand. Hide what exactly?<br /> <br /> O, sweet. He has stats somewhere? I really like him so if you could point me the right direction it would be great.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:31:54-07:00","id":1067141,"title":"","content":"The scene with the Nemean worked because no one checked to see if anyone else was an imposter, didn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T13:51:05-07:00","id":1067154,"title":"","content":"It was skipped so we can't really tell but I think it was the case, yea. Since I think it is retarded to not check for veils if you conspire, for the sake of the thread I assumed that they did and didn't pierce his potency. In 1e it meant that there might be something but most likely nothing. Which is different from 2E and I wanted to talk about it here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:00:07-07:00","id":1067194,"title":"","content":"They thought they'd been sneakier, mages are still people and you can take advantage of their overconfidence is the lesson I'd take from that. The Nemean had probably lulled them into a false sense of security beforehand by giving the appearance of turning a blind eye to their machinations instead of jumping them right from the beginning of their plot. They would have started paranoid and jumping at everything, but eventually the fear would wear off. Then the Nemean made his move.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T15:31:34-07:00","id":1067209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067139#post1067139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I don't understand. Hide what exactly?<br /> <br /> O, sweet. He has stats somewhere? I really like him so if you could point me the right direction it would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>His stats are in the 1e corebook. As for hiding, hide the spell from Peripheral Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T19:32:55-07:00","id":1067320,"title":"","content":"This is the old problem of meta-game thinking; players roll dice and figure that means something had to happen.<br /> \u200bThis is something the ST has to deal with and the easiest way is to first hide his dice whenever rolling in apparent opposition, then make it clear that he is going to roll those dice anytime you ask him to, even if there is nothing there for his roll to represent.<br /> <br /> Player-&quot;I got a success! What did I find?&quot;<br /> ST-&quot;Nothing.&quot;<br /> Player-&quot;He beat my roll?&quot;<br /> ST-&quot;Or there was nothing there to find, you don't know.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bThe player can even add Willpower dice to the roll, all the time knowing he may be wasting them on a snipe hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T21:19:43-07:00","id":1067382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067320#post1067320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the old problem of meta-game thinking; players roll dice and figure that means something had to happen.<br /> \u200bThis is something the ST has to deal with and the easiest way is to first hide his dice whenever rolling in apparent opposition, then make it clear that he is going to roll those dice anytime you ask him to, even if there is nothing there for his roll to represent.<br /> <br /> Player-&amp;quot;I got a success! What did I find?&amp;quot;<br /> ST-&amp;quot;Nothing.&amp;quot;<br /> Player-&amp;quot;He beat my roll?&amp;quot;<br /> ST-&amp;quot;Or there was nothing there to find, you don't know.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bThe player can even add Willpower dice to the roll, all the time knowing he may be wasting them on a snipe hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not applicable to CoW. The latter explicitly requires another supernatural ability to be opposing your own. The only exception I can think of is Incognito Presence, in which case the spell makes you forget seeing the person should you have seen them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T02:18:31-07:00","id":1067462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067320#post1067320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the old problem of meta-game thinking; players roll dice and figure that means something had to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meta isn't a problem, but the way it's handled might be. Also, characters explicitly know when a CoW happens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 03-24-2017, 05:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T02:58:10-07:00","id":1067467,"title":"","content":"I'd just say Prime can veil a CoW from the other party. <br /> <br /> Or Mind, I guess","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T03:36:42-07:00","id":1067474,"title":"","content":"Fate could be used to lower the chances of being checked with AMS in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T03:49:44-07:00","id":1067479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067320#post1067320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the old problem of meta-game thinking; players roll dice and figure that means something had to happen.<br /> \u200bThis is something the ST has to deal with and the easiest way is to first hide his dice whenever rolling in apparent opposition, then make it clear that he is going to roll those dice anytime you ask him to, even if there is nothing there for his roll to represent.<br /> <br /> Player-&quot;I got a success! What did I find?&quot;<br /> ST-&quot;Nothing.&quot;<br /> Player-&quot;He beat my roll?&quot;<br /> ST-&quot;Or there was nothing there to find, you don't know.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bThe player can even add Willpower dice to the roll, all the time knowing he may be wasting them on a snipe hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been playing roughly ten years now, and I can handle meta-gaming just fine. As long as the character isn't drugged, crazy or under magical attack that induces false alarms CoW can't ping randomly. It is a direct confrontation roll, not a perception roll.<br /> <br /> Player-&quot;I got a success! <b>Did I hit him</b>?&quot;<br /> ST-&quot;Nope.&quot;<br /> Player-&quot;He beat my roll?&quot;<br /> ST-&quot;Or <b>there was nothing there to hit</b>, you don't know.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sounds quite weird if it isn't part of the plot or enemies ability.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:00:41-07:00","id":1067483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067467#post1067467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd just say Prime can veil a CoW from the other party.<br /> <br /> Or Mind, I guess</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, I wrote such a spell. You can find it on the first page if this thread.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> That could help too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:06:36-07:00","id":1067486,"title":"","content":"Prime could screw with the area's Resonance so their Sanctum is flooded with Trust, or you could go Astral diving beforehand, raid their Oneiros and turn off or down whatever apparatus is in there that allows them to recognize enemies, etc.<br /> <br /> Really, when infiltrating a Mage does better when they prepare ahead of time instead of relying on just a Veil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:09:06-07:00","id":1067487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067194#post1067194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They thought they'd been sneakier, mages are still people and you can take advantage of their overconfidence is the lesson I'd take from that. The Nemean had probably lulled them into a false sense of security beforehand by giving the appearance of turning a blind eye to their machinations instead of jumping them right from the beginning of their plot. They would have started paranoid and jumping at everything, but eventually the fear would wear off. Then the Nemean made his move.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmm. Conflict in mage requires assumption that parties are incompetent. Otherwise players can't do much or die from the first hit. It's like the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> always says, better to turn you mages against the world and not the other mages who is extremely hard and dangerous. I kind of feel like this should be written somewhere in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067209#post1067209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> His stats are in the 1e corebook. As for hiding, hide the spell from Peripheral Sight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Veiling spells are automatically hidden from PMS.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:09:49-07:00","id":1067488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067483#post1067483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes, I wrote such a spell. You can find it on the first page if this thread.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> That could help too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw it, I thought it was quite good<br /> <br /> That said I'm curious as to why you think a GM wouldn't allow it. A CoW is caused by two supernatural effects colliding and Mages know their spells are being clashed. The purview is clearly that of Prime (potentially Mind as well, because throught at knowledge) because it's magic and also because it relates to controlling Truth, which Prime covers. It's clearly a veiling effect, too.<br /> <br /> So put the two together and you get a perfectly legitimate Prime Veiling spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:19:33-07:00","id":1067490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067486#post1067486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Prime could screw with the area's Resonance so their Sanctum is flooded with Trust, or you could go Astral diving beforehand, raid their Oneiros and turn off or down whatever apparatus is in there that allows them to recognize enemies, etc.<br /> <br /> Really, when infiltrating a Mage does better when they prepare ahead of time instead of relying on just a Veil.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really nice ideas, but both are spells.Changing resonance by leylines might not be terribly effective but on the other hand it can actually work, kind of like 50/50. And can be investigated. Not likely but can.<br /> When messing with Oneiros you must cast spells inside of it, right? I mean that you can't modify it without spell for too long. So you can conjure some magical seal inside but it can still be detected with prime. Or. You can damage it and hope it won;t regenerate too fast. Second option is really cool and could make a great Chapter. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:26:36-07:00","id":1067492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067487#post1067487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Conflict in mage requires assumption that parties are incompetent. Otherwise players can't do much or die from the first hit. It's like the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> always says, better to turn you mages against the world and not the other mages who is extremely hard and dangerous. I kind of feel like this should be written somewhere in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't require incompetence, it's more like Shadowrun where you are probably going to die if you don't do as much research into your enemy as possible before making a move and if you really want to succeed you need to discover a weak spot from which to target your approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T04:48:34-07:00","id":1067500,"title":"","content":"If you are going to infiltrate a conspiracy of several potent Mages planning treachery against the Hierarch with the intention of committing a bit of brutal violence on them then you'd better be a cunning, powerful and nasty piece of work to pull it off.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for him, the Nemean is all of that, plus a 2nd degree Master with various other Arcana...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:00:51-07:00","id":1067552,"title":"","content":"I'm not clear on exactly which part of the Nemean fiction you're not able to recreate in 2E. Many Faces not a Veiling spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:19:59-07:00","id":1067561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>galivet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067552#post1067552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not clear on exactly which part of the Nemean fiction you're not able to recreate in 2E. Many Faces not a Veiling spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Many Faces being an active non-Veiling spell would ping PMS (Depending on your interpretation) which could lead to scrutiny. You could Veil it, but then you might get CoW if they decide to check you with AMS which could tip them off. That's the problem Moinen is having I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:23:05-07:00","id":1067562,"title":"","content":"Funny thing, if active spells were more common and pinging PMS in presence of other mages, hiding such thing in a plain sight would be much easier. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:29:49-07:00","id":1067565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067562#post1067562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny thing, if active spells were more common and pinging PMS in presence of other mages, hiding such thing in a plain sight would be much easier. </div> </div> </div> </div>True, and I really don't see a reason why they wouldn't be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:30:07-07:00","id":1067566,"title":"","content":"Yeah I think that's worth considering; Mages in that situation will be warding themselves extensively, including probably veiling the location in Space, Time, maybe Fate etc to avoid snooping. Those veiling spells, if they pinged PMS, would mean you wouldn't be noticing a ping from Many Faces.<br /> <br /> Which is quite cunning, really. Makes things a bit more interesting. To infiltrate you don't want to veil necessarily, you want other options, whose presence then fades into the background hum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:32:27-07:00","id":1067570,"title":"","content":"Is PMS precise enough to tell you how many spells are around that person anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:34:32-07:00","id":1067573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nor does Peripheral Mage Sight give any clues as to what just happened \u2014 only that magic is afoot. </div> </div> </div>It doesn't even tell you directly what Arcana are in play.<br /> <br /> Most every mage walk around with active effects. <i>Of course</i> Thanatos's cabalmates sense that &quot;Thanatos&quot; has some active effect going. He <i>always</i> does. <i>Every </i>mage does. What raises suspicion about it? They would have just assumed that &quot;Thanatos&quot; had Soul Armor or something active.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","user":"galivet","date":". 03-24-2017, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T07:35:11-07:00","id":1067574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067570#post1067570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is PMS precise enough to tell you how many spells are around that person anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without a merit, wasn't there one for SoS that lets you detect arcana used via PMS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:00:19-07:00","id":1067588,"title":"","content":"There is one such merit in the preview, yeah. There's another that lets you know if it's something you've sensed before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:00:57-07:00","id":1067590,"title":"","content":"Even if there was, conceivably that wouldn't look dodgy at all. Hey guys the guy with Life is using a Life spell!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-24T08:08:48-07:00","id":1067594,"title":"","content":"Heck, you'd probably have decent luck using Many Faces to look like neither yourself or the guy you're pretending to be and then just convince your &quot;friends&quot; that they're not being paranoid -enough-, and that &quot;you&quot;-ve changed your face to keep their secrets safe. You have to layer your deceptions with Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T04:07:38-07:00","id":1067959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067488#post1067488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I saw it, I thought it was quite good<br /> <br /> <b>That said I'm curious as to why you think a GM wouldn't allow it.</b> A CoW is caused by two supernatural effects colliding and Mages know their spells are being clashed. The purview is clearly that of Prime (potentially Mind as well, because throught at knowledge) because it's magic and also because it relates to controlling Truth, which Prime covers. It's clearly a veiling effect, too.<br /> <br /> So put the two together and you get a perfectly legitimate Prime Veiling spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that might be &quot;the mages know, and are absolute detectives&quot; part of setting. *shrug* but maybe it isn't so controversial to change as I thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067562#post1067562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny thing, if active spells were more common and pinging PMS in presence of other mages, hiding such thing in a plain sight would be much easier.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is actually a question about common sense and what customs would emerge from world working as it works (from mechanics). So. <b>Let's talk customs. </b><br /> <br /> PMS is tingling for every non veiling or veiled spell that is in vicinity. Is it irritating? What is vicinity? Does it go off for your spells?<br /> Every ping is a potential attack.<br /> Mage is always aware of CoW. He is not aware if he won, which would be weird but lets say.<br /> Sanctum is a place guarded by golden laws. Sacred and safe.Every<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1. If Peripheral is irritating it means that all magic in Sanctum should be veiled for cabalmates to not get crazy.<br /> 2. If it's not irritating it could mean that after a while it becomes something like fridge buzz or a clock ticking, something that you are only aware when thinking about.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">a. you can't detect any of the other magic</div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">b. you can distinguish between familiar buzz and something new</div><b>Host - Guest situation</b><br /> 1. First option leaves us with quiet Sanctums which shouldn't be disturbed by a lot of spells. You should drop them when entering. I don't think that this option is possible. There are spells that can't be dropped, augmentations, temporarily repaired disabilities and gender issues. It must mean that Peripheral is not irritating, otherwise mages would hate other mages.<br /> <br /> 2.a All spells should be veiled - it's an equivalent of setting the alarm in case of burglary. You can't detect supernatural attack if it hums constantly. When you are a guest you must drop all active effects and ask for permission for every spell you cast inside to make sure that the host is aware whats happening.<br /> <br /> 2.b Spells in sanctum don't have to be veiled but still you should ask for permission to cast a spell in somebodies house. Kind of like with smoking. Still every ping can be a potential attack on privacy or well being. Generally don't do it, it's uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> <br /> The common thread is that you shouldn't cast without asking first. It's rude. Leave your wizard staff at threshold to not disturb the sanctum. No mage sight without asking first or being told to.<br /> <br /> <b>Q: </b>What is a range of PMS?<br /> &quot;an Aimed spell\u2019s short range is Gnosis x 10, medium is Gnosis x 20, and long is Gnosis x 40.&quot; Maybe this could help. If we go with medium it is still encompassing whole sanctum. No hiding.<br /> <br /> Can it go through walls? I don't know. Help me with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:44:21-07:00","id":1067978,"title":"","content":"PMS range is sensory, I know we had a conversation about that earlier in another thread.<br /> <br /> A guest leaving their Yantras at the door does seem like it would be a common courtesy. At the very least it curtails the damage they can do if things turn sour. Although you can't disarm a Mage of High Speech and Mudras. A vow in High Speech to stay your hand and tongue could work though, since you can't lie in High Speech. You could change your mind later of course, but then there would be a record of you breaking your word.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T05:54:47-07:00","id":1067982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067978#post1067978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PMS range is sensory, I know we had a conversation about that earlier in another thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, I remember something. But if it's an extra sense it could not care for walls. The same if it can be perceived with normal senses, hearing for example. Do spells hum or you can't perceive them until affected by them?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A guest leaving their Yantras at the door does seem like it would be a common courtesy. At the very least it curtails the damage they can do if things turn sour. Although you can't disarm a Mage of High Speech and Mudras. A vow in High Speech to stay your hand and tongue could work though, since you can't lie in High Speech. You could change your mind later of course, but then there would be a record of you breaking your word. </div> </div> </div>High Speech seems to be a great indicator of someone intentions. There should be even some traditional formula of &quot;I come with no ill intentions... bla bla bla&quot;. And those who lie in HS by using spell should be severely punished.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:14:44-07:00","id":1067984,"title":"","content":"If a spell is hidden behind a wall you would only notice it via PMS if it provided some other sort of sensory information.<br /> <br /> Hmm...I kind of feel like I may be coming around to the opinion that everything just works better if PMS only goes off when the spell is cast instead of over the course of the spell's entire Duration...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:23:24-07:00","id":1067987,"title":"","content":"Irritating / not irritating depends on the individual Peripheral Sights (if your PMS takes a form of headache, then well; if it's the sexiest laughter you ever heard, then well), but I assume that magic is in general pleasant experience to both cast and witness for a Mage, unless it's specifically designed to be somehow unpleasant or the Mage in question is a Banisher. &quot;Magic as a drug&quot; and so on. If so, it would be actually another mechanism pushing Mages to congregate, because being with other Mages = having your Sight gently caressed = pleasure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:25:39-07:00","id":1067988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067984#post1067984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a spell is hidden behind a wall you would only notice it via PMS if it provided some other sort of sensory information.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you can't detect shit. Spells and powers used in Twilights go unnoticed. Vampires Auspex goes unnoticed. Knowing practices generally go unnoticed. AMS also. Some Moros shapes stack of coin into a swan in her purse? No sound, no sight input. Nothing.<br /> Only thing you could perceive is a fireball. &quot;Yup, thats a spell, I'm telling you Mike. Swear to god that my sixth sense is tingling.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmm...I kind of feel like I may be coming around to the opinion that everything just works better if PMS only goes off when the spell is cast instead of over the course of the spell's entire Duration... </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking about it too but didn't make up my mind yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":1747,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","user":"Moinen","date":". 03-25-2017, 09:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:33:28-07:00","id":1067990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067984#post1067984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a spell is hidden behind a wall you would only notice it via PMS if it provided some other sort of sensory information.<br /> <br /> Hmm...I kind of feel like I may be coming around to the opinion that everything just works better if PMS only goes off when the spell is cast instead of over the course of the spell's entire Duration...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why we homeruled that spells ping when<br /> A) They go off<br /> B) They make an active impact - Shielding Spell get's it's shield challenged by something, Accelerated Mage uses their super speed, and so on<br /> <br /> It works pretty OK in practice for what we wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T06:37:20-07:00","id":1067991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1066567-on-infiltrations?p=1067987#post1067987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Irritating / not irritating depends on the individual Peripheral Sights (if your PMS takes a form of headache, then well; if it's the sexiest laughter you ever heard, then well), but I assume that magic is in general pleasant experience to both cast and witness for a Mage, unless it's specifically designed to be somehow unpleasant or the Mage in question is a Banisher. &quot;Magic as a drug&quot; and so on. If so, it would be actually another mechanism pushing Mages to congregate, because being with other Mages = having your Sight gently caressed = pleasure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think that I'll put in my design doc. Doing Magic is a pleasant and addictive feeling (mostly).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T07:13:22-07:00","id":1067998,"title":"","content":"I don't remember if that's in the books or if it's something we homebrewed, but I remember that we ran this way since 1st ED.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:54:51-07:00","id":1068104,"title":"","content":"Does using or activating an attainment set off PMS?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T14:58:38-07:00","id":1068105,"title":"","content":"Yes. Without going into when PMS should ping I can definitely say attainments are not exempt from PMS since it's a supernatural effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T15:17:16-07:00","id":1068107,"title":"","content":"PMS is one of these things that would work really well in a video game, but is little harder for me to utilize in tabletop. I try to give each character at least one &quot;detailed&quot; PMS description per game, with their preferred flavor (there is a person who loves creepy stuff so she gets goosebumpey sightings, while other dude gets more of a curious doctor whoisz ding), and boil most of the other instances to just &quot;it pings your PMS&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}